From a3705004a5dc46c4f22cf5cabd6a114dd2074df7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:30:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] fix(ewm): subject is the grammatical holder; supersession
 only for same present state or a corrected past event

Root cause fixed in Ewm1Fact.subject itself (was: first capitalised word):
'ich'/'wir' of the first clause, else the first mention that is no
sentence-initial time/update adverb. subjectKnown is false for reported or
quoted speech and coordinated subjects; such facts neither replace nor get
replaced. The possessive gender cue skips pronoun subjects.

Ewm1Memory.replaces() now separates three relations explicitly:
SUPERSEDES_STATE (same holder and predicate, present tense, single-valued
or update/correction), CORRECTS_EVENT ('nicht ..., sondern ...' for the same
past event and time anchor), COEXISTS (everything else). A shared entity or
two time anchors count only when neither statement names a predicate of its
own (appointments). Past/historical statements never end a present state;
future states do not either. Lexicon: PAST/FUTURE/PRESENT cues, degree words,
verbs of saying.

Ewm1Workspace.current() follows a known supersession through the memory even
when retrieval returned only the old fact, so an outdated fact is never
presented as current.

